        "met_days": 304,
        "type": "arrival",
        "label": "Mars orbit insertion",
        "description": "1976-06-19. The orbiter captured Viking 1 into Mars orbit and spent a month imaging candidate lander sites — the original Chryse Planitia target proved too rough, so the team re-targeted from orbit."
      },
      {
        "met_days": 335,
        "type": "edl_or_oi",
        "label": "Viking 1 Mars touchdown — Chryse Planitia",
        "description": "1976-07-20 — the 7th anniversary of Apollo 11. First successful US Mars surface landing (the Soviet Mars 3 landed in 1971 but operated for only 15 seconds). Viking 1 returned high-resolution colour panoramas + the first biological-experiment results (ambiguous to this day) + 6 years of meteorological data. Lasted until 1982-11-11."
      }
